1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,561
Hey techies! Sneha here

2
00:00:02,561 --> 00:00:04,364
from Zillenial Talk.

3
00:00:04,364 --> 00:00:06,167
Season 1, episode 3.

4
00:00:06,467 --> 00:00:07,206
Nobody sat down

5
00:00:07,206 --> 00:00:07,990
and wrote a rule

6
00:00:07,990 --> 00:00:08,866
for how your email

7
00:00:08,866 --> 00:00:09,743
knows what's spam.

8
00:00:10,043 --> 00:00:11,043
So how does it know?

9
00:00:11,693 --> 00:00:12,645
Think about teaching

10
00:00:12,645 --> 00:00:13,325
a toddler what

11
00:00:13,325 --> 00:00:13,778
a cat is.

12
00:00:14,078 --> 00:00:14,959
You don't hand

13
00:00:14,959 --> 00:00:15,957
them a rulebook.

14
00:00:15,957 --> 00:00:16,838
You just point

15
00:00:16,838 --> 00:00:17,718
at cats, again

16
00:00:17,718 --> 00:00:18,364
and again.

17
00:00:18,664 --> 00:00:19,513
Soon, they spot

18
00:00:19,513 --> 00:00:20,575
a cat they've never

19
00:00:20,575 --> 00:00:21,265
seen before.

20
00:00:21,915 --> 00:00:22,977
That's the core idea

21
00:00:22,977 --> 00:00:23,534
behind AI.

22
00:00:23,834 --> 00:00:25,369
Instead of programmers writing

23
00:00:25,369 --> 00:00:26,508
every rule, the system

24
00:00:26,508 --> 00:00:27,796
learns patterns from lots

25
00:00:27,796 --> 00:00:28,440
of examples.

26
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:30,166
That's how spam filters,

27
00:00:30,166 --> 00:00:31,993
photo search and chatbots work.

28
00:00:32,643 --> 00:00:34,260
Now, the toddler comparison

29
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:34,952
has limits.

30
00:00:35,252 --> 00:00:36,919
A toddler understands what

31
00:00:36,919 --> 00:00:37,537
a cat is.

32
00:00:37,537 --> 00:00:38,648
AI finds patterns

33
00:00:38,648 --> 00:00:39,636
in data, and it

34
00:00:39,636 --> 00:00:41,241
can be confidently wrong.

35
00:00:41,891 --> 00:00:42,863
So AI is software

36
00:00:42,863 --> 00:00:43,998
that learns patterns

37
00:00:43,998 --> 00:00:44,808
from examples,

38
00:00:44,808 --> 00:00:45,618
not just rules

39
00:00:45,618 --> 00:00:46,428
a human wrote.

40
00:00:46,728 --> 00:00:48,433
Not so scary now, right?

41
00:00:48,733 --> 00:00:50,078
One tech concept.

42
00:00:50,078 --> 00:00:51,422
One simple story.

43
00:00:51,422 --> 00:00:52,916
I'm Sneha, and this

44
00:00:52,916 --> 00:00:54,336
is Zillenial Talk.

